<title>CHILE: Chile November forex reserves rise to $15.26 bln.</title>
<headline>Chile November forex reserves rise to $15.26 bln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's international reserves rose $68 million in November to $15.26 billion, the central bank said in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>The increase is the result of a $71 million rise in the balance of payments account and a $3 million fall in the value of the reserves as the result of international exchange rate fluctuations, it said.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago Newsroom 562-699-5595x212</p>
